-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell I17's ORDER twin, graded as its own row.  Byte-identical to
-- main.mdk except the two interface-module import lines are swapped.  Reordering import
-- clauses is cosmetic -- every formatter and every reviewer treats it that way -- so the
-- two rows must agree, and a program whose meaning depends on the difference is wrong
-- whatever the right answer turns out to be.
--
-- Before the fix these two files disagreed about whether the program COMPILES: main.mdk
-- accepted at exit 0 printing 7, this one was rejected `Type mismatch: Int vs String`.
--
-- ⚠️ A PAIR IS WEAKER THAN A PERMUTATION DIFFERENTIAL: three import clauses have six
-- orderings and this pins two.  The other four are NOT owed --
-- `test/import_order_fixtures/1351-methoddispatchidx-import-order-collision/` is this same
-- graph in the permutation corpus, and this fix DRAINED its ledger row, so it now runs
-- UNLEDGERED there and must stay invariant across all six.  These two rows are the
-- SEMANTIC companion to that one: they say WHY the answer is 99 -- neither interface is
-- nameable in the entry -- and pin the VALUE on all three verbs, which an invariance check
-- alone cannot, because six orderings agreeing on a WRONG value is also invariant.
import fmodI.{mth}
import zmodI.{zf}
import amodI.{af}

